--- !u!114 &372825415
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 372825412}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a11dd23e08e5cb942a6a6b4da8d43711, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: TEXDrawRuntime::TexDrawLib.TEXDraw
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 0, g: 0, b: 0, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_Alignment: {x: 0.5, y: 0.5}
  m_Text: "That\u2019s Correct!\r\n\r\nThe marbles in the bag are:\r\n\r\n2 black,
    3 blue, 4 yellow, and 1 green\r\n\r\nLet\u2019s list the total number of marbles:\r\n\r\n2
    + 3 + 4 + 1 = 10 marbles\r\n\r\nSince the marbles are selected randomly, each
    marble has an equal chance of being chosen.\r\n\r\nLet\u2019s define the events:\r\n\r\nEvent
    A: The first marble selected is green\r\n\r\nEvent B: The second marble selected
    is yellow\r\n\r\nFirst, we find the probability of selecting a green marble on
    the first draw.\r\n\r\nThere is 1 green marble out of 10 total marbles.\r\n\r\nP(A)
    = \\frac{1}{10}\r\n\r\nSince the marble is not replaced, there are now 9 marbles
    left in the bag.\r\n\r\nOriginally there were 4 yellow marbles, and none were
    removed if the first marble was green.\r\n\r\nSo there are still 4 yellow marbles
    out of 9 remaining marbles.\r\n\r\nP(B) = \\frac{4}{9}\r\n\r\nWe can calculate
    the probability using the formula:\r\n\r\nP(A \\text{ and } B) = P(A) \\times
    P(B)\r\n\r\nP(A \\text{ and } B) = \\frac{1}{10} \\times \\frac{4}{9}\r\n\r\nP(A
    \\text{ and } B) = \\frac{4}{90}\r\n\r\nP(A \\text{ and } B) = \\frac{2}{45}\r\n\r\nSo,
    the probability that the first marble selected is green and the second marble
    selected is yellow is \\frac{2}{45} or about 0.044 or 4.44\\%.\r\n\r\nThere are
    4 favorable outcomes out of 90 possible ordered outcomes for the two selections,
    so the chance of selecting a green marble first and a yellow marble second is
    \\frac{2}{45}."
  m_Size: 6
  m_ScrollArea:
    serializedVersion: 2
    x: 0
    y: 0
    width: 0
    height: 0
  m_Padding:
    left: 10
    right: 10
    top: 10
    bottom: 10
  m_Overflow: 0
